WEBVTT

00:00:00.000 --> 00:00:04.220
Bando Gym

00:00:07.850 --> 00:00:11.020
I set my alarm wrong! It's past 10AM!

00:00:13.100 --> 00:00:16.390
Kazu! W-We're late for the qualifiers!

00:00:16.390 --> 00:00:17.970
It's 6:01! It's 6:01!

00:00:17.970 --> 00:00:21.140
Good morning to you on this very chilly day!

00:00:21.140 --> 00:00:23.720
Huh? It's still 6AM?

00:00:23.720 --> 00:00:29.180
Haru, you didn't wake up at all while
I messed around with your alarm clock.

00:00:29.180 --> 00:00:31.060
Give me a break!

00:00:31.060 --> 00:00:33.640
Good morning! You should
hurry up and eat, too!

00:00:33.640 --> 00:00:36.220
Your food is still the best, Miharu!

00:00:36.220 --> 00:00:37.930
Here, these bento are for you.

00:00:37.930 --> 00:00:39.430
Thank you very much!

00:00:41.060 --> 00:00:45.600
I put extra effort into making these
today, so eat up and work hard!

00:00:45.600 --> 00:00:46.220
We will!

00:00:46.220 --> 00:00:49.100
Mom, about the cheerleading...

00:00:49.100 --> 00:00:51.720
Good luck at the qualifiers!

00:00:51.720 --> 00:00:53.600
Thank you.

00:00:58.770 --> 00:00:59.930
Morning.

00:00:59.930 --> 00:01:03.220
Good morning! Will you eat with us, Haruko?

00:01:04.520 --> 00:01:06.220
I'll eat later.

00:01:08.810 --> 00:01:12.100
Sorry about that. She hasn't
been feeling well lately.

00:01:12.100 --> 00:01:13.970
What do you mean?

00:01:13.970 --> 00:01:15.430
You see...

00:01:15.430 --> 00:01:19.060
Haruko's been on a losing streak.

00:01:36.680 --> 00:01:42.350
<i>I'll put an end to spending</i>
<i>my days so thoughtlessly</i>

00:01:42.350 --> 00:01:46.430
<i>I'm dying to break free of this</i>

00:01:46.430 --> 00:01:52.140
<i>Since I can never take that first step forward,</i>

00:01:52.140 --> 00:01:56.220
<i>you always take my hand and pull me along</i>

00:01:56.220 --> 00:02:02.060
<i>You've brought me to see</i>
<i>something completely new</i>

00:02:02.060 --> 00:02:04.350
<i>My whole world is changing</i>

00:02:04.350 --> 00:02:07.560
<i>With that first step</i>

00:02:07.560 --> 00:02:10.720
<i>I felt transformed</i>

00:02:10.720 --> 00:02:15.680
<i>I can go anywhere; it'll work</i>
<i>out so long as we're together</i>

00:02:15.680 --> 00:02:17.270
<i>Go on, fly high, </i>

00:02:17.270 --> 00:02:18.890
<i>just as you are</i>

00:02:18.890 --> 00:02:22.060
<i>At times you'll feel lost and scared,</i>

00:02:22.060 --> 00:02:28.600
<i>but there are so many things you</i>
<i>won't know if you never give them a go</i>

00:02:28.600 --> 00:02:30.220
<i>Go on, fly high, </i>

00:02:30.220 --> 00:02:35.100
<i>stretch out your hands until</i>
<i>you're almost touching the sky</i>

00:02:35.100 --> 00:02:38.350
<i>We're not alone anymore</i>

00:02:38.350 --> 00:02:43.470
<i>Together we'll fly into a new world</i>

00:02:51.890 --> 00:02:53.900
National Cheerleading Championship

00:02:51.890 --> 00:02:53.900
<b>Kanto Qualifiers</b>

00:02:53.900 --> 00:02:56.150
National Cheerleading Championship

00:02:53.900 --> 00:02:56.150
<b>Kanto Qualifiers</b>

00:02:57.350 --> 00:02:58.850
First of all, everyone calm d--

00:02:58.850 --> 00:03:01.060
It's gettin' tense!

00:03:02.850 --> 00:03:05.600
They all looking at me or something?

00:03:05.600 --> 00:03:09.310
Aren't their eyes glued to your poofy hair?

00:03:09.310 --> 00:03:12.060
Really? Good thing I went with an afro!

00:03:12.060 --> 00:03:14.600
A team full of dudes must be a rare sight.

00:03:14.600 --> 00:03:17.020
'Round and 'round... They're still
rolling 'round and 'round...

00:03:17.020 --> 00:03:18.770
Did you overeat today, too?

00:03:18.770 --> 00:03:21.770
Bro, I need to go to the bathroom.

00:03:21.770 --> 00:03:24.970
You still haven't broken that nervous habit.

00:03:24.970 --> 00:03:26.930
It's no good, I feel faint.

00:03:26.930 --> 00:03:29.310
I-I'm going back home to the country.

00:03:29.310 --> 00:03:34.890
H-How pathetic. This is the performance of a
lifetime. Let's man up and die glorious deaths!

00:03:34.890 --> 00:03:36.930
Let's skip the dyin' part.

00:03:38.100 --> 00:03:41.020
Look! Those girls' ribbons are so cute!

00:03:46.310 --> 00:03:48.600
Pull yourselves together, boys!

00:03:48.600 --> 00:03:50.890
Disgraceful. Stop panicking!

00:03:50.890 --> 00:03:52.100
Coach!

00:03:52.100 --> 00:03:53.930
Good morning!

00:03:53.930 --> 00:03:56.520
Good morning. Everyone's here, right?

00:03:56.520 --> 00:03:58.020
Right!

00:03:58.020 --> 00:03:59.060
Let's get moving!

00:03:59.060 --> 00:04:00.310
Yeah!

00:04:04.100 --> 00:04:05.100
Hm?

00:04:06.270 --> 00:04:07.770
Haru! We're going!

00:04:07.770 --> 00:04:10.100
Huh? Y-Yeah!

00:04:14.930 --> 00:04:21.020
The base score needed to qualify for our
university student division is 80 points.

00:04:21.020 --> 00:04:25.560
If we don't make any big mistakes, we should
be able to pass with our routine just fine.

00:04:25.560 --> 00:04:26.520
Right!

00:04:26.520 --> 00:04:31.180
Well, the opening ceremony will start soon,
so let's get ready and move to the venue.

00:04:31.180 --> 00:04:33.640
Thank you very much!

00:04:36.270 --> 00:04:39.020
It's okay. Concentrate. You can do it.

00:04:39.020 --> 00:04:40.270
--Concentrate. Concentrate.
--Hey, Ha--

00:04:40.270 --> 00:04:43.220
Concentrate. Concentrate. Concentrate.

00:04:43.220 --> 00:04:45.180
--Con... Con...
--What's wrong with Haru?

00:04:45.180 --> 00:04:46.770
--Con carne. Chili con carne.
--He's scaring me.

00:04:46.770 --> 00:04:49.390
--That sounds good. Chili...
--He's as fragile as a normal person.

00:04:49.390 --> 00:04:51.310
--Con... Con...
--H-Haru?

00:04:51.310 --> 00:04:53.060
Huh? What?!

00:04:54.640 --> 00:04:57.770
Uh, I'm going to the bathroom.
You guys go ahead!

00:05:00.390 --> 00:05:01.560
Tokugawa!

00:05:06.140 --> 00:05:07.270
Who's that?

00:05:07.270 --> 00:05:09.390
He comes that annoyin' guy...

00:05:09.390 --> 00:05:12.680
Looks like you finally got the
nerve to take center stage.

00:05:12.680 --> 00:05:18.020
But don't think an all-men's
team like yours can beat us!

00:05:19.020 --> 00:05:21.470
Who are you?

00:05:21.470 --> 00:05:23.890
Wait, you don't know him?

00:05:23.890 --> 00:05:27.100
Sho, he's from Sparks. His name is, uh...

00:05:27.100 --> 00:05:33.350
I'm Kaoru Hanasaki, the superstar-god
miracle-ace who showed up on Sparks

00:05:33.350 --> 00:05:36.060
like a comet after
you quit cheerleading!

00:05:36.060 --> 00:05:38.640
So what do you want?

00:05:38.640 --> 00:05:44.060
Today I'll prove to you that Sparks with
me on it is the strongest team here!

00:05:44.060 --> 00:05:45.970
Hanasaki, cool it.

00:05:52.470 --> 00:05:55.470
Domoto... It's been a while.

00:05:55.470 --> 00:05:59.140
Yes. I'm happy you came back to cheerleading.

00:05:59.140 --> 00:06:01.680
I'm looking forward to today's performance.

00:06:01.680 --> 00:06:03.180
Thanks.

00:06:03.180 --> 00:06:05.140
Let's beat everyone today!

00:06:05.140 --> 00:06:06.220
Yeah!

00:06:08.890 --> 00:06:12.430
Haruko's been on a losing streak.

00:06:12.430 --> 00:06:14.390
Haru!

00:06:14.390 --> 00:06:16.100
Long time no see!

00:06:16.100 --> 00:06:20.220
Hm? Are you okay? You don't look so good.

00:06:20.220 --> 00:06:23.020
No, I'm fine. Thanks.

00:06:23.020 --> 00:06:24.470
I'll sit with you.

00:06:26.350 --> 00:06:29.890
Your first official tournament
is so nerve-wracking, isn't it?

00:06:29.890 --> 00:06:32.680
I was nervous, too. Almost got a nosebleed!

00:06:32.680 --> 00:06:34.430
Really?

00:06:34.430 --> 00:06:39.350
We've both practiced hard for this day,
so I hope we make it a complete success!

00:06:40.430 --> 00:06:43.180
Haru? You really are out of it.

00:06:43.180 --> 00:06:45.430
--Ah, sorr--
--Haru!

00:06:45.430 --> 00:06:47.350
The opening ceremony is starting!

00:06:47.350 --> 00:06:49.020
Oh no, I have to go!

00:06:49.020 --> 00:06:51.560
Well, let's both do our best!

00:06:55.680 --> 00:06:58.560
So you had time for a rendezvous
before our performance.

00:06:58.560 --> 00:07:02.930
Huh? BBQ? Oh, is there
hamburger in our bento?

00:07:04.140 --> 00:07:08.180
H-Haru, are you all right? If it's
about what you heard this morning...

00:07:09.220 --> 00:07:10.850
I know, already.

00:07:11.890 --> 00:07:13.470
Concentrate, right?

00:07:16.060 --> 00:07:21.560
...Right.

00:07:21.560 --> 00:07:27.020
The National Cheerleading Championship's
Kanto Qualifiers will now begin!

00:07:33.430 --> 00:07:37.350
Remember one thing before you go out there.

00:07:37.350 --> 00:07:41.470
Not a single person here today is your enemy.

00:07:41.470 --> 00:07:46.520
They're allies cheering you on.
Winning or losing isn't the important thing.

00:07:46.520 --> 00:07:50.220
It's doing your best performance for yourself.

00:07:50.220 --> 00:07:51.390
Right!

00:07:52.600 --> 00:07:54.680
We'll definitely win the next one!

00:07:54.680 --> 00:07:57.680
It's fine... I know she'll be fine...

00:08:00.060 --> 00:08:02.020
Haru, deep breaths!

00:08:02.020 --> 00:08:06.770
I know you've got a lot on your mind,
but just focus on cheerleading for now.

00:08:06.770 --> 00:08:08.640
Kazu...

00:08:08.640 --> 00:08:11.810
It's okay, Haruko can do it. Please!

00:08:11.810 --> 00:08:13.310
Y-Yeah!

00:08:16.100 --> 00:08:19.350
Next up are the Breakers
from Meishiin University!

00:08:19.350 --> 00:08:20.220
Let's do this!

00:08:20.220 --> 00:08:21.350
Yeah!

00:08:27.560 --> 00:08:30.470
Concentrate... Concentrate...

00:08:43.220 --> 00:08:45.680
My winning streak ended.

00:08:45.680 --> 00:08:49.680
Haruko's been on a losing streak.

00:08:49.680 --> 00:08:51.310
Sis...

00:08:52.970 --> 00:08:54.180
Ready!

00:09:09.560 --> 00:09:11.220
Haru!

00:09:12.810 --> 00:09:15.890
C'mon, don't let it keep you down.

00:09:22.890 --> 00:09:26.020
Hisashi, how did I do today?

00:09:26.020 --> 00:09:29.810
That small mistake really
stood out. It's not like you.

00:09:29.810 --> 00:09:32.770
Ah, you're right. I'm sorry.

00:09:32.770 --> 00:09:35.100
I'm so happy we passed!

00:09:35.100 --> 00:09:37.350
That was tense, Bro.

00:09:37.350 --> 00:09:39.930
It was nothing like being on a dance stage.

00:09:39.930 --> 00:09:45.560
We just barely slid safe into base score
range. Welp, passing is a win for me!

00:09:45.560 --> 00:09:48.810
I pulled off my turn so much
better than I thought I would!

00:09:48.810 --> 00:09:52.140
But we still have quite a ways to go.

00:09:52.140 --> 00:09:55.140
We passed the qualifiers thanks
to everybody's hard work.

00:09:55.140 --> 00:09:58.850
Let's congratulate ourselves now,
and start practicing again tomorrow.

00:09:58.850 --> 00:10:02.220
Even on the big stage, your
performance was solid, Sho.

00:10:02.220 --> 00:10:07.640
No, I was pretty nervous, too.
I'm so glad it went well.

00:10:07.640 --> 00:10:10.930
Kazu, Sho, we're going to fill out
the application for the finals.

00:10:10.930 --> 00:10:11.970
Right!

00:10:11.970 --> 00:10:13.640
Then we'll see you tomorrow!

00:10:15.680 --> 00:10:19.390
Make sure you put the
acceptance slip somewhere safe.

00:10:19.390 --> 00:10:20.270
Will do.

00:10:20.270 --> 00:10:22.140
Well done.

00:10:22.140 --> 00:10:23.850
Oh, Domoto.

00:10:23.850 --> 00:10:25.060
You did great.

00:10:25.060 --> 00:10:26.390
Well...

00:10:26.390 --> 00:10:29.180
Congratulations on passing the qualifiers.

00:10:29.180 --> 00:10:30.520
Thank you.

00:10:30.520 --> 00:10:33.890
Though I have mixed feelings about
hearing that from the captain of the team

00:10:33.890 --> 00:10:35.560
that put on today's best performance.

00:10:35.560 --> 00:10:37.720
Not at all.

00:10:37.720 --> 00:10:40.140
Congratulations to you, too, Sho.

00:10:40.140 --> 00:10:41.810
Thank you very much!

00:10:41.810 --> 00:10:46.180
But I don't approve of
your team's cheerleading.

00:10:46.180 --> 00:10:49.100
The Breakers' cheerleading is a circus.

00:10:49.100 --> 00:10:53.640
You've certainly got the hang of it,
and you can do stunts relatively well.

00:10:53.640 --> 00:10:58.560
But you still fail to understand the most
important thing about cheerleading.

00:10:58.560 --> 00:11:00.350
Excuse me.

00:11:16.770 --> 00:11:18.640
Stop!

00:11:18.640 --> 00:11:21.140
That's all wrong! Do it again!

00:11:21.140 --> 00:11:25.600
Are you serious about this? The National
Championship is less than a month away!

00:11:25.600 --> 00:11:28.390
Sho, how about a quick break?

00:11:28.390 --> 00:11:30.930
We don't have time for that!

00:11:30.930 --> 00:11:35.350
Without a perfect, more high-level
performance, we'll fall flat at the Nationals!

00:11:35.350 --> 00:11:40.350
That may be true, but if we overdo it
and get hurt, this'll all be for nothing!

00:11:40.350 --> 00:11:45.350
But at this rate, we're hopeless!
We'll just get called a circus...again!

00:11:45.350 --> 00:11:47.100
Sho...

00:11:49.270 --> 00:11:52.640
Say, hasn't Sho been weird lately?

00:11:52.640 --> 00:11:55.520
He's certainly been on edge
ever since the qualifiers ended.

00:11:55.520 --> 00:11:58.180
And he headed right home again today, too.

00:11:58.180 --> 00:11:59.640
Did something happen?

00:11:59.640 --> 00:12:02.100
Sho's not the only one acting weird.

00:12:03.640 --> 00:12:05.270
Good work today.

00:12:05.270 --> 00:12:06.270
Later.

00:12:07.640 --> 00:12:10.060
He left wearin' that again.

00:12:10.060 --> 00:12:12.890
But no one can pry about it anymore.

00:12:19.270 --> 00:12:21.430
Oh, Takagi!

00:12:21.430 --> 00:12:24.270
Ah, doing your Sunday shopping together?

00:12:24.270 --> 00:12:27.350
We're on our way back from
cheering for the baseball club.

00:12:27.350 --> 00:12:30.970
Uh... I...

00:12:32.020 --> 00:12:34.770
I'm sorry for butting in the other day.

00:12:34.770 --> 00:12:39.100
What's up? Why're you hanging your head?

00:12:39.100 --> 00:12:42.100
You must be sincere if
you're apologizing like that.

00:12:42.100 --> 00:12:44.810
How is he doing?

00:12:44.810 --> 00:12:48.720
If you mean Sho, it seems
like he's back to his old self.

00:12:48.720 --> 00:12:50.060
Is he?

00:12:50.060 --> 00:12:53.770
Sho? What's happened to that Tokugawa guy?

00:12:53.770 --> 00:12:57.220
Uh, not that I particularly care or anything.

00:12:57.220 --> 00:13:03.890
I think he did well to pass the qualifiers with
an amateur team. I mean, I'm not worried at all.

00:13:03.890 --> 00:13:08.890
Cheerleading is still torture for Sho.

00:13:08.890 --> 00:13:13.350
Well, I mean, he did cause that accident.
It was his own fault.

00:13:13.350 --> 00:13:15.020
It wasn't.

00:13:15.020 --> 00:13:18.270
That accident wasn't just Sho's fault.

00:13:29.930 --> 00:13:31.770
H-Hold on!

00:13:31.770 --> 00:13:33.930
There's nobody here!

00:13:33.930 --> 00:13:34.930
Huh?

00:13:34.930 --> 00:13:37.640
What am I supposed to do with these?

00:13:37.640 --> 00:13:40.020
Ah, it's cold!

00:13:42.140 --> 00:13:46.100
Hm? What's this? A Risujiro fair?

00:13:48.060 --> 00:13:50.220
You worked hard today.

00:13:50.220 --> 00:13:54.430
My students are about to take their general
entrance exams, so everyone's on edge.

00:13:54.430 --> 00:13:56.520
They rival our Drill Captain.

00:13:56.520 --> 00:13:57.970
What, me?

00:13:57.970 --> 00:14:03.100
The other guys are saying that you've gotten
pretty Spartan ever since the qualifiers ended.

00:14:03.100 --> 00:14:07.810
You do understand that the Nationals are
out of reach at our current level, right?

00:14:07.810 --> 00:14:10.680
I don't really have any complaints.

00:14:10.680 --> 00:14:13.720
Everyone's worried about you, Sho.

00:14:13.720 --> 00:14:19.810
I've come to realize that not asking what's
wrong isn't always the right thing to do.

00:14:20.890 --> 00:14:22.140
Kazu...

00:14:22.140 --> 00:14:25.140
If you're struggling with
something all by yourself,

00:14:25.140 --> 00:14:27.640
then I want you to let us support you, too.

00:14:28.970 --> 00:14:34.890
Sakura and I were in awe of Domoto.

00:14:34.890 --> 00:14:37.140
Yes, that's perfect!

00:14:37.140 --> 00:14:41.350
Jin, please teach us the
Walk-In Extension next!

00:14:41.350 --> 00:14:46.140
Not so fast. Take it slow
and start with the Step-Up.

00:14:46.140 --> 00:14:50.140
If we don't hurry, then won't you graduate?

00:14:50.140 --> 00:14:53.140
I'll be waiting for you on
the university Sparks team.

00:14:53.140 --> 00:14:57.390
So wrap up the Summer Cup
for your age bracket with a win!

00:14:57.390 --> 00:15:00.390
Yes! We'll definitely get first place!

00:15:00.390 --> 00:15:03.270
Make sure you come watch us!

00:15:04.180 --> 00:15:09.850
After you left, Sakura and Sho
became Captain and Drill Captain,

00:15:09.850 --> 00:15:12.430
and threw themselves into practice.

00:15:12.430 --> 00:15:16.810
They inspired everyone around them,
and the team's skill level improved.

00:15:16.810 --> 00:15:19.640
Back then, everybody who
did high school cheerleading

00:15:19.640 --> 00:15:22.890
knew about the Tokugawa-Takagi duo.

00:15:24.770 --> 00:15:27.220
Just before the Summer Cup...

00:15:27.220 --> 00:15:31.270
We're going to raise the
overall difficulty of our stunts.

00:15:31.270 --> 00:15:32.390
Starting now?

00:15:32.390 --> 00:15:34.680
The Summer Cup is next week!

00:15:34.680 --> 00:15:37.930
We need to challenge
ourselves in order to win.

00:15:37.930 --> 00:15:42.020
I know we can do it! We'll definitely win!

00:15:42.930 --> 00:15:46.560
You don't understand what's
important about cheerleading.

00:15:46.560 --> 00:15:48.430
What do you mean?

00:15:48.430 --> 00:15:51.430
Your cheerleading is a circus.

00:15:53.180 --> 00:15:56.520
1, 2, 3, 4!

00:15:56.520 --> 00:15:58.600
That's all wrong! Do it again!

00:15:58.600 --> 00:16:03.270
Flyer! Your cradle posture is weak!
It's just a flashy circus act like that!

00:16:03.270 --> 00:16:04.350
Right.

00:16:04.350 --> 00:16:07.640
Base, you're off-center during the catch!
Your stunts lack precision!

00:16:07.640 --> 00:16:08.890
I'm sorry.

00:16:08.890 --> 00:16:12.600
Our technical score won't improve
with difficult stunts alone!

00:16:12.600 --> 00:16:17.140
Without a perfect, more high-level
performance, we can't win!

00:16:17.140 --> 00:16:19.890
We aren't putting on a circus!

00:16:21.560 --> 00:16:23.310
Cheerleading Summer Cup

00:16:29.600 --> 00:16:31.180
Sho...

00:16:32.930 --> 00:16:37.930
I helped cause that accident. I'm truly sorry.

00:16:37.930 --> 00:16:43.600
I've told you countless times that that's
not true. Come now, lift up your head.

00:16:43.600 --> 00:16:47.770
I take great pride in cheerleading
competitions that hone one's skills.

00:16:47.770 --> 00:16:51.890
But that doesn't mean I've forgotten
cheerleading's fundamental goal.

00:16:54.270 --> 00:16:57.410
ＹＯＭＥＩ ＨＩＧＨ ＳＣＨＯＯＬ ＢＵＳ ＳＴＯＰ

00:16:59.890 --> 00:17:04.060
This time I have to put on a
perfect, high-level performance,

00:17:04.060 --> 00:17:07.060
and prove to Domoto that I'm okay now.

00:17:07.060 --> 00:17:09.390
Sho...

00:17:09.390 --> 00:17:14.220
Is that what Domoto really meant
when he said it was a circus?

00:17:15.270 --> 00:17:17.930
Is that what cheerleading is?

00:17:22.970 --> 00:17:26.310
Tokugawa! How long do you
plan on moping around?!

00:17:26.310 --> 00:17:27.390
Uh?

00:17:27.390 --> 00:17:30.100
W-Welcome...?

00:17:31.140 --> 00:17:32.060
Who are you?

00:17:32.060 --> 00:17:34.720
Kaoru Hanasaki from Sparks!

00:17:34.720 --> 00:17:37.890
You make me sick!

00:17:37.890 --> 00:17:43.310
Just how worried do you think everyone is?
Aren't they rooting for you?

00:17:43.310 --> 00:17:47.220
Don't make them so anxious!
Get real and put their minds at ease!

00:17:47.220 --> 00:17:50.850
Domoto, and Coach Takagi, and Sakura, too!

00:17:50.850 --> 00:17:52.970
And then take on me!

00:17:52.970 --> 00:17:54.390
Sho.

00:17:55.560 --> 00:17:59.520
Didn't Domoto want to
say it made him anxious?

00:17:59.520 --> 00:18:06.060
That a circus-like performance makes the
audience worry about how dangerous it is?

00:18:06.060 --> 00:18:10.930
Just like you guys did for me, the most
important thing in cheerleading is

00:18:10.930 --> 00:18:14.850
supporting your audience
and making them smile, right?

00:18:14.850 --> 00:18:17.060
Domoto said that earlier, too.

00:18:17.060 --> 00:18:19.020
But that's just no good.

00:18:19.020 --> 00:18:20.140
Sho?

00:18:20.140 --> 00:18:26.060
We have to put on a perfect performance
at the Nationals. Or else I can't face Sakura!

00:18:26.060 --> 00:18:27.930
You're still hung up on that?

00:18:27.930 --> 00:18:29.470
That's not true!

00:18:29.470 --> 00:18:31.390
What would you know, Haru?!

00:18:31.390 --> 00:18:35.770
Sakura is rooting for you even now!

00:18:35.770 --> 00:18:38.060
I heard about it from Coach Takagi.

00:18:38.060 --> 00:18:43.520
Sakura asked her to to send her those
practice videos she's always taking!

00:18:43.520 --> 00:18:46.560
Keep it a secret from him for now.

00:18:46.560 --> 00:18:48.850
I'll explain everything another time.

00:18:50.180 --> 00:18:51.850
Sho...

00:18:51.850 --> 00:18:54.180
Go to Sakura and talk to her.

00:18:59.810 --> 00:19:02.220
I wonder if Sho will be able
to talk to her properly.

00:19:02.220 --> 00:19:05.020
Feel like you could, Haru?

00:19:05.020 --> 00:19:09.180
Who's the person you want to
make smile most right now?

00:19:32.310 --> 00:19:33.720
Sho!

00:19:33.720 --> 00:19:35.100
What in the world's going on?

00:19:35.100 --> 00:19:37.720
I, uh...

00:19:37.720 --> 00:19:39.770
I came to see Sakura.

00:19:42.720 --> 00:19:45.640
She's been waiting a long time.

00:19:55.560 --> 00:19:56.770
Come in!

00:20:03.720 --> 00:20:04.970
Sis?

00:20:15.310 --> 00:20:17.720
You still have zero fashion sense!

00:20:20.060 --> 00:20:22.350
Hey, Sho! Look at me!

00:20:23.720 --> 00:20:27.100
I'm pretty pissed, y'know.

00:20:27.100 --> 00:20:30.180
Ain't it outrageous that you quit
cheerleading without asking me?

00:20:30.180 --> 00:20:32.100
Yes! I'm sorry!

00:20:32.100 --> 00:20:37.770
I decided if you were going to go hide and sulk,
then I'd have to find you and drag you out.

00:20:37.770 --> 00:20:39.310
Sakura!

00:20:39.310 --> 00:20:43.770
I've been overdoing it with my
rehabilitation, so I'll be walking soon!

00:20:52.520 --> 00:20:55.470
Still only good at the catch, aren't you?

00:21:00.020 --> 00:21:01.270
Is that...?

00:21:01.270 --> 00:21:02.270
Oh!

00:21:03.390 --> 00:21:04.600
Why?

00:21:06.470 --> 00:21:09.680
I've been watching you this whole time.

00:21:09.680 --> 00:21:13.350
Seeing you do cheerleading has inspired me.

00:21:16.270 --> 00:21:20.270
Sakura... I'm so sorry for
everything that happened.

00:21:20.270 --> 00:21:24.180
I'll be sure to cheer for you at the
National Championship on my own two feet!

00:21:28.970 --> 00:21:32.020
Yeah. Thank you.

